  "details": "I have a slightly custom video player in one of my worlds which plays pre-defined videos when a user inserts a cartridge in an NES:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_a2c7017d-95be-4829-adde-47ba50dc08be\nThe video player was working fine until a recent update. I have not modified the world since I first uploaded it a few months ago, so either something about how the youtube DLL functions changed which is affecting video players, or something changed about Udon which is now causing the code to malfunction.\nSome of the cartridges work fine, until you insert one which doesn't, and then the video player breaks and you have to create a new instance to get it to function again.\nFor example the TMNT cartridge sitting on top of the NES, and the Rescue Rangers cartridge in the stack to the right of the TV are broken and inserting either breaks the player. But Zelda, Super C, and Ducktales work correctly.\nI checked the URLs for the two broken cartridges and the videos are still on Youtube, so it's not a case of a video being taken down causing the issue, but here are the URLs for them if you need to test:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k4MjHpc25eg\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k5E_c4hI83k\nThere are more broken videos than just those two, those are just the ones I know for sure off the top of my head.",
